# FIEL AL LIBRO — sample translation template
# This is a WORKING EXAMPLE of the key convention and file format.
# Regenerate with:
#   godot --headless --script res://src/tools/extract_strings.gd
#
# FORMAT: gettext PO, with two Godot-specific rules.
#
#  - NO msgctxt. Godot 4.7 creates the key "context<U+0004>msgid" but leaves
#    the VALUE EMPTY, so a contextual string can never be translated. Put
#    the context in the key name instead: ui.word.page.book,
#    ui.word.page.nav, character.quixote.
#  - NO msgid_plural. Godot exposes only msgstr[0]; msgstr[1+] are dropped,
#    and a file using msgid_plural is rejected unless the header carries a
#    valid "Plural-Forms" line. There is no ngettext. The plural form is
#    its own ordinary key: ui.shelf.count.plural.
# RULES:
#   - Never translate the msgid. Never use the source text as a key.
#   - Translator comments start with "TRANSLATORS:" (shown to translators) or
#     "# META:" (metadata for the tooling, hidden from translators).
#   - MAXLEN comments are hints for fixed-width UI slots. Leave 35% slack.

